lead=dict(key='leadership',slug='fde-for-leaders',title='Forward Deployment Engineering for Leaders',shortTitle='FDE for Leaders',image='ai-leadership',headline='Lead AI from a promising demo to a governed decision.',intro='A C-suite learning experience for selecting useful AI opportunities, funding bounded pilots, assigning ownership and making evidence-based decisions about adoption.',audience='C-suite leaders, business heads and transformation sponsors',bridge='No coding prerequisite. Bring familiarity with a business workflow, its stakeholders and the decisions you need to make. Technical concepts are explored through demonstrations, proposal reviews and leadership exercises.',scope='Adapted from the original Forward Deployed AI Leadership curriculum. This is leadership preparation rather than the engineer coding track. The 90-day blueprint is a planning exercise, not a course duration or a guaranteed delivery schedule.',tags=['AI strategy','Pilot economics','Governance','Adoption'],paths=[['Business sponsors','Frame value, baseline measures, decision rights and the investment case for a bounded pilot.'],['Technology & transformation leaders','Connect architecture, data readiness, risk ownership and operating-model decisions.']],modules=[
module('AI reality for leaders','brain','Evaluate proposals by capability, evidence and consequences of error.','LLM capabilities, unsupported answers and limitations|RAG, fine-tuning and smaller-model tradeoffs|Agents, reversible actions and human approval|Voice, vision and document-workflow opportunities','Facilitated model demonstrations — inspect success and failure|Capability scorecard — compare a proposal with evidence|Workflow map — locate decisions and escalation','Review a proposal claiming AI can resolve all service tickets. Narrow the ticket classes, permitted actions and evidence requirements, then request a denied-action and unsupported-answer demonstration.','AI proposal review|Capability/limitation map|Human-control boundary','The proposal has testable scope|Consequential actions have review owners|A fluent demonstration is not treated as proof of reliability'),
module('Prioritise & fund','target','Choose an opportunity the organisation can responsibly validate.','Workflow discovery and measurable baselines|Data quality, provenance and permission readiness|Build, buy and partner comparisons|Cost assumptions, review effort and sensitivity analysis','Use-case scorecard — compare value, feasibility and risk|Spreadsheet scenario model — test cost/value assumptions|Vendor-question guide — examine integration and exit needs','Compare an internal knowledge assistant, invoice triage and a sales-support workflow. Select one bounded pilot and explain why the alternatives should wait.','Opportunity shortlist|Build/buy/partner rationale|Assumption-based value and cost model','Value is tied to a stated baseline|Review, integration and operating costs are included|Estimates are scenarios rather than promised returns'),
module('Govern & operate','shield','Assign responsibility for safe operation and meaningful adoption.','Risk, human control and stop conditions|Access limits, logs and necessary evidence|Business, technical and incident ownership|Role-specific training, feedback and change management','Risk register — identify owners and controls|RACI — clarify decision and operating responsibilities|Tabletop incident exercise — rehearse escalation|Adoption checklist — define readiness evidence','Map an approval-based invoice workflow. Rehearse an incorrect recommendation, an unauthorised action and an unavailable service, then decide who pauses the pilot.','Risk/control register|Operating model and escalation map|Adoption and feedback plan','Reviewers have evidence, time and authority|Logs do not unnecessarily expose sensitive content|An accountable owner can stop or revise the workflow'),
module('The 90-day execution blueprint','compass','Present an evidence-led pilot plan with a genuine stop or scale decision.','Priority use cases and dependency sequencing|Pilot audience, quality measures and baseline|Data, evaluation, user-readiness and incident gates|Leadership review, scope revision and controlled expansion','Pilot charter — scope the experiment|Decision-gate checklist — define evidence and ownership|Executive narrative — present the recommendation|Roadmap template — sequence discovery, pilot and review','Present an illustrative 90-day plan: first establish the baseline and permissions, then run a bounded pilot, then review measured evidence. Explain what would change your recommendation.','Pilot charter|Phased roadmap with owners|Executive decision brief','Efficiency measures are paired with quality and risk measures|Dates are planning assumptions, not delivery promises|Stop, revise and scale decisions each have explicit evidence')],projects=[
project('AI opportunity investment brief','target','Leadership has several attractive proposals but limited delivery capacity.','Workflow baseline|Readiness scorecard|Options|Pilot recommendation','Compare three illustrative opportunities and present the assumptions behind one priority.','Benefits counted twice|Data rights unclear|Vendor capability mistaken for organisational readiness','Use-case scorecard|Cost assumptions|Decision memo'),
project('A governed operations pilot','shield','Invoice triage could reduce repetitive work, but a wrong action has consequences.','Approved documents|AI suggestion|Human approval|Operational record','Design the review boundary, ownership and stop conditions using a simulated workflow.','Approval without sufficient evidence|Unauthorised access|No incident owner','Control matrix|Tabletop incident notes|Operating-model proposal'),
project('The executive deployment blueprint','compass','A successful demonstration needs a controlled path into organisational practice.','Discover|Bound the pilot|Evaluate|Stop / revise / scale','Prepare and defend a 90-day planning scenario with measurable gates, adoption responsibilities and a handover decision.','Metrics reward speed but hide errors|Users cannot challenge output|Scaling before readiness','Pilot charter|Adoption roadmap|Executive presentation')],preparation=[['Challenge AI proposals','Ask for baselines, failure examples, access boundaries and a clear operating owner.'],['Lead an investment conversation','Explain value assumptions, total operating effort and what evidence would justify further funding.'],['Rehearse governance decisions','Practise pausing or revising a pilot when quality, risk or adoption evidence is inadequate.'],['Communicate a deployment decision','Present the charter, accountable owners and stop/scale criteria to business and technical stakeholders.']])
